.policy "django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change" revision 1
.description "Give a data migration that writes rows its own migration, apart from schema changes to the same table; on PostgreSQL one shared transaction can fail or lock the table."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. On PostgreSQL a migration runs in one transaction unless it sets `atomic = False`,
// RunPython included (RunPython's own `atomic=False` takes effect only in a non-atomic migration: Migration.apply).
// Django's RunPython docs: "avoid combining schema changes and RunPython operations in the same migration or you may
// hit errors like OperationalError: cannot ALTER TABLE "mytable" because it has pending trigger events". Reported, at
// the RunPython, when its function (in the migration or imported, and the functions of the run it calls) binds
// `apps.get_model("app", "M")` (or "app.M") to a name and writes M's rows through it: `.objects…update/create/
// bulk_create/bulk_update/delete/get_or_create/update_or_create`, `M(...).save()`, or `save()`/`delete()` on rows
// fetched from it; and an operation of the same migration that changes the database alters M's table (AddField,
// AlterField, RemoveField, RenameField, Add/Remove/RenameIndex, Add/RemoveConstraint, AlterUniqueTogether,
// AlterIndexTogether, AlterModelTable, RenameModel, DeleteModel; a SeparateDatabaseAndState's database_operations):
//   - PendingTriggerEvents, the alteration after the RunPython: the writes queue deferred foreign-key checks on M's
//     table (Django creates foreign keys DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED), and PostgreSQL refuses to alter a table with
//     checks pending. Only writes that queue a check count (PostgreSQL skips the check when a key is unchanged):
//     inserting rows into a model with a foreign key (create, bulk_create, get_or_create, update_or_create,
//     `M(...).save()`), setting a foreign key (`update(customer=…)`, `bulk_update(…, ["customer"])`,
//     `obj.customer_id = …` then save), or deleting rows a foreign key or many-to-many field points at. A foreign key
//     an AddField earlier in the same migration added does not count: Django adds it `SET CONSTRAINTS … IMMEDIATE`;
//     nor does one the later operation alters or removes itself: Django first runs `SET CONSTRAINTS <it> IMMEDIATE`;
//     nor any, when `SET CONSTRAINTS ALL IMMEDIATE` runs between the writes and the alteration (a RunSQL between
//     them, or a string of the RunPython's own code: DefectDojo's `0286_cicd_infrastructure.py`), which runs the
//     queued checks.
//       RunPython(merge_duplicate_customers)   # deletes customers orders point at
//       AlterField("customer", "email", models.EmailField(unique=True))          reported
//   - LockedBackfill, the alteration before the RunPython: its ACCESS EXCLUSIVE (or SHARE, for an index) lock lasts
//     until the migration commits, so the table stays locked for the whole backfill. Not when every write touches
//     one row once (rps_one): a write on a row fetched with get()/first()/last() or filtered by an exact
//     lookup on a unique column (the primary key, a field the migrations make unique), or a single insert, with no
//     loop around it in its def or around the call into its def. Such a lock is held for milliseconds.
//       AddField("order", "number", models.CharField(null=True)); RunPython(fill_order_numbers)    reported
// Left alone: migrations with `atomic = False`; squashed migrations (`replaces`), which run on new databases; a run
// that configures MySQL and names no PostgreSQL database (MySQL commits each DDL statement); a model the same
// migration creates (its table is new, and its foreign keys are added at the end); before the RunPython, a model the
// project's code reads as one row (dj_one_row: `M.objects.get()`, a lazy-singleton `first()` beside a `create()`,
// `M.get_solo()`), a settings table;
// RunPython code that only reads M, or writes another model than the one altered; an AlterField that changes only
// attributes Django keeps out of the database (choices, help_text, verbose_name, blank, default, validators, ...),
// judged against the field's nearest earlier definition in the app's migrations; after the RunPython, writes that
// queue no check (an update of other columns, an insert into a model without foreign keys, a delete of rows nothing
// points at); RunPython.noop and reverse code; RunSQL; state_operations; migrations in test directories.
//       RunPython(clear_notes)   # Order.objects.update(note="")
//       AlterField("order", "note", ...)                                         not reported
// Gaps: a model is matched by its lowercased name, not its app label; a model name held in a variable that is not a
// loop over literal names, or a model passed to a helper, is not followed, nor writes through related managers
// (`order.tags.add()`), raw SQL (`schema_editor.execute("DELETE …")`) or a helper more than one call deep. Foreign
// keys are read from the run's migrations and models by name, so one of another app's same-named model counts. An
// update of rows an earlier operation of the same transaction rewrote queues checks even with unchanged keys; such a
// migration is reported as LockedBackfill. Whether a backfill is long depends on the table's size, which the rule
// cannot see (hence log mode, off by default); a team that migrates with the application stopped pays only upgrade
// time, not an outage.
// The RunPython's functions, the migration history and the models are in several files, so the rule reads them by
// symbol and by key (decision 0691): each def states by its qualified name what it writes (rps_w, rps_ins, rps_set,
// ...), each migration its operations by its key (rps_run, rps_alt, rps_rel), each field call its class and arguments
// as values (rps_vcls, rps_vkw, rps_vpos); the orders are decided over those, and the output reads the answer back at
// the RunPython by its key, item and function.

#include "lib/django.rerail"

.violation PendingTriggerEvents(at: node, m: symbol) "This RunPython queues foreign-key checks on {m}, and PostgreSQL refuses the later ALTER of it. Split the migration, or RunSQL SET CONSTRAINTS ALL IMMEDIATE before the ALTER; leave applied migrations."
PendingTriggerEvents(o, m) :- rps_rp(o, _, i, q), dj_key_of(o, k), rps_after(k, i, q, m), !dj_mysql_only().

.violation LockedBackfill(at: node, m: symbol) "An earlier operation locks {m} until the migration commits, so the table stays locked through this backfill. Move the RunPython into its own migration; keep it for a small table or an applied one."
LockedBackfill(o, m) :- rps_rp(o, _, i, q), dj_key_of(o, k), rps_before(k, i, q, m), !rps_after(k, i, q, m),
    !dj_mysql_only().

// ---- the RunPython and the defs it runs ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rps_rp(o, d, i, q): RunPython o, item i of migration d, runs the function named q in d's one transaction: d is
// atomic, not a squash, not test code. A run that configures MySQL alone (dj_mysql_only, a fact about the whole
// repository) is left out in the outputs.
.decl rps_rp(o: node, d: number, i: number, q: symbol)
rps_rp(o, d, i, q) :- dj_runpython(o, d, i, q), !dj_mig_nonatomic(d), !dj_test_doc(d), !dj_mig_attr(d, "replaces", _).
// rps_run(k, i, q): the same by the migration's key.
.decl rps_run(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol)
rps_run(k, i, q) :- rps_rp(o, _, i, q), dj_key_of(o, k).
// rps_def(k, i, q, h): def h runs as the code of RunPython item i of migration k, function q: q itself, or a def of the
// run q calls (dj_calls). rps_looped(k, i, q, h): q calls h from a loop, so each of h's writes runs many times.
.decl rps_def(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol, h: symbol)
rps_def(k, i, q, q) :- rps_run(k, i, q).
rps_def(k, i, q, h) :- rps_run(k, i, q), dj_calls(q, h).
.decl rps_looped(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol, h: symbol)
rps_looped(k, i, q, h) :- rps_run(k, i, q), rps_loop_calls(q, h).
// rps_loop_calls(g, h): def g calls def h of the run from a loop in its body (rps_in_loop). Stated in g's file.
.decl rps_loop_calls(g: symbol, h: symbol)
rps_loop_calls(gq, hq) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), qualname(g, gq), rps_in_loop(c, g), field(c, "function", e),
    sym_of(e, hq), docof(c, d), doc(d, p, _), py_names__reads_at(p, m), py_names__defined(m, hq).
// rps_in_loop(c, h): call c runs in a loop of def h (a for or while statement, a comprehension).
.decl rps_in_loop(c: node, h: node)
rps_in_loop(c, h) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), kind(c, "call"), within(c, s), within(s, h),
    (kind(s, "for_statement") ; kind(s, "while_statement") ; kind(s, "list_comprehension") ;
    kind(s, "generator_expression") ; kind(s, "set_comprehension") ; kind(s, "dictionary_comprehension")).

// ---- the rows each def writes ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rps_get_model(c, s): call c is `apps.get_model("app", "S")`, `get_model(model_name="S")` or `get_model("app.S")`.
.decl rps_get_model(c: node, s: symbol)
rps_get_model(c, s) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "get_model"), posarg(c, 1, n), str(n, s).
rps_get_model(c, s) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "get_model"),
    call_arg(c, -1, "model_name", n), str(n, s).
rps_get_model(c, s) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "get_model"), posarg(c, 0, n),
    !posarg(c, 1, _), !call_arg(c, -1, "model_name", _), str(n, q), split_dot(q, _, s).
// A model name held in a loop variable over literal names resolves to each of them:
//   for name in ["Order", "Invoice"]: M = apps.get_model("shop", name)      rps_get_model(<call>, "Order"), (…, "Invoice")
rps_get_model(c, s) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "get_model"),
    (posarg(c, 1, n) ; call_arg(c, -1, "model_name", n)), kind(n, "identifier"), text(n, y),
    kind(l, "for_statement"), within(c, l), field(l, "left", v), kind(v, "identifier"), text(v, y),
    field(l, "right", r), (kind(r, "list") ; kind(r, "tuple")), child(r, e, _), str(e, s).

// rps_model(h, x, m): scope h binds name x to the historical model m (lowercased).
.decl rps_model(h: node, x: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_model(h, x, @lower(s)) :- asg(h, x, v, _), unparen(v, c), rps_get_model(c, s).

// rps_chain_method(a): querysets methods whose result still holds model rows (values() and values_list() hold dicts
// and tuples, whose `update()` is no write).
.decl rps_chain_method(a: symbol)
rps_chain_method(a) :- dj_qs_method(a), a != "values", a != "values_list".
rps_chain_method(a) :- dj_row_method(a).
rps_chain_method("iterator").

// rps_from(e, h, m, how): in def h, e is model m (how "model"), one of its querysets or fetched rows ("rows"), or an
// instance built in h ("new").
.decl rps_from(e: node, h: node, m: symbol, how: symbol)
rps_from(e, h, m, "model") :- rps_model(h, x, m), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x), look(e, x, h).
rps_from(e, h, m, how) :- rps_name(h, y, m, how), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, y), look(e, y, h).
rps_from(e, h, m, "rows") :- attr_of(e, o, a), dj_manager_name(a), rps_from(o, h, m, "model").
rps_from(e, h, m, "rows") :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, a), rps_chain_method(a),
    rps_from(o, h, m, "rows").
rps_from(e, h, m, "new") :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), rps_from(f, h, m, "model").
rps_from(e, h, m, how) :- kind(e, "parenthesized_expression"), unparen(e, u), rps_from(u, h, m, how).

// rps_name(h, y, m, how): def h binds y to such a value: `y = <rps_from>`, or `for y in <rps_from>:`.
.decl rps_name(h: node, y: symbol, m: symbol, how: symbol)
rps_name(h, y, m, how) :- asg(h, y, v, _), unparen(v, e), rps_from(e, h, m, how).
rps_name(h, y, m, how) :- kind(s, "for_statement"), field(s, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, y),
    field(s, "right", r), unparen(r, e), rps_from(e, h, m, how), how != "model", nearest(s, h, scope).

// rps_write(h, c, m, w, how): call c, in def h, writes rows of model m through method w on a queryset or fetched row
// (how "rows") or a built instance ("new").
.decl rps_write(h: node, c: node, m: symbol, w: symbol, how: symbol)
rps_write(h, c, m, w, how) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), kind(c, "call"), within(c, h), field(c, "function", f),
    attr_of(f, u, w), rps_write_method(w), unparen(u, e), rps_from(e, h, m, how), how != "model".
.decl rps_write_method(w: symbol)
rps_write_method("update"). rps_write_method("create"). rps_write_method("bulk_create").
rps_write_method("bulk_update"). rps_write_method("delete"). rps_write_method("get_or_create").
rps_write_method("update_or_create"). rps_write_method("save").
// rps_insert_method(w): the write methods that can insert rows.
.decl rps_insert_method(w: symbol)
rps_insert_method("create"). rps_insert_method("bulk_create"). rps_insert_method("get_or_create").
rps_insert_method("update_or_create").

// What each def states of its writes, by its qualified name h, for the cross-file part:
//   rps_w(h, c, m)         write c (its term, pt_tm) writes rows of m
//   rps_ins(h, m)          h inserts rows of m: create, bulk_create, get_or_create, update_or_create, `M(...).save()`
//   rps_del(h, m)          h deletes rows of m
//   rps_set(h, m, a)       h sets attribute a of m's rows: an update()/update_or_create() keyword, a bulk_update()
//                          field name
//   rps_save(h, m)         h saves rows of m (`.save()`)
//   rps_assign(h, m, a)    h assigns `y.a = …` on a row y of m
//   rps_sets_all(h)        a string in h is `SET CONSTRAINTS ALL IMMEDIATE`
.decl rps_w(h: symbol, c: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_w(hq, ct, m) :- rps_write(h, c, m, _, _), qualname(h, hq), pt_tm(c, ct).
.decl rps_ins(h: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_ins(hq, m) :- rps_write(h, _, m, w, _), rps_insert_method(w), qualname(h, hq).
rps_ins(hq, m) :- rps_write(h, _, m, "save", "new"), qualname(h, hq).
.decl rps_del(h: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_del(hq, m) :- rps_write(h, _, m, "delete", _), qualname(h, hq).
.decl rps_set(h: symbol, m: symbol, a: symbol)
rps_set(hq, m, a) :- rps_write(h, c, m, w, _), (w = "update" ; w = "update_or_create"), call_arg(c, -1, a, _),
    qualname(h, hq).
rps_set(hq, m, a) :- rps_write(h, c, m, "bulk_update", _), call_arg(c, _, _, l), child(l, s, _), str(s, a),
    qualname(h, hq).
.decl rps_save(h: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_save(hq, m) :- rps_write(h, _, m, "save", _), qualname(h, hq).
.decl rps_assign(h: symbol, m: symbol, a: symbol)
rps_assign(hq, m, t) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), kind(a, "assignment"), within(a, h), field(a, "left", l),
    attr_of(l, y, t), rps_from(y, h, m, how), how != "model", qualname(h, hq).
.decl rps_sets_all(h: symbol)
rps_sets_all(hq) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), kind(s, "string"), within(s, h), str(s, t),
    match("(?is).*set\\s+constraints\\s+all\\s+immediate.*", t), qualname(h, hq).

// ---- one row once -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rps_w_one(h, c, um, uk): write c in def h touches one row and runs once in h's own code (no loop around it in h): a
// write on one fetched row (rps_single), an insert of one row (`create`, `get_or_create`, `update_or_create`,
// `M(...).save()`). Sure when um is ""; else only when keyword uk names one row of model um (rps_unique_lookup, which
// the run's migrations decide). Whether h itself runs in a loop of the RunPython's function is rps_looped's.
//   Order.objects.filter(pk=1).update(status="legacy")     rps_w_one(_, _, "", "")
//   owner = Customer.objects.get(email=…); owner.save()    rps_w_one(_, _, "customer", "email")
.decl rps_w_one(h: symbol, c: symbol, um: symbol, uk: symbol)
rps_w_one(hq, ct, "", "") :- rps_write(h, c, _, _, "rows"), rps_receiver(c, e), rps_single(e, h), !rps_in_loop(c, h),
    qualname(h, hq), pt_tm(c, ct).
rps_w_one(hq, ct, um, uk) :- rps_write(h, c, _, _, "rows"), rps_receiver(c, e), rps_single_if(e, h, um, uk),
    !rps_in_loop(c, h), qualname(h, hq), pt_tm(c, ct).
rps_w_one(hq, ct, "", "") :- rps_write(h, c, _, w, _), rps_insert_method(w), !rps_in_loop(c, h), qualname(h, hq),
    pt_tm(c, ct).
rps_w_one(hq, ct, "", "") :- rps_write(h, c, _, "save", "new"), !rps_in_loop(c, h), qualname(h, hq), pt_tm(c, ct).
// rps_receiver(c, e): e is what method call c is called on.
.decl rps_receiver(c: node, e: node)
rps_receiver(c, e) :- field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, u, _), unparen(u, e).
// rps_single(e, h): in def h, e is one row of a model, or a queryset of at most one: a `get()` (Django raises on
// two rows), `first()`, `last()`, `latest()`, `earliest()`; a `filter()`/`get()` with an exact lookup on the primary
// key (`pk`, `id`, with or without `__exact`); the chain methods after one; a name bound to one.
// rps_single_if(e, h, m, k): the same where the lookup is keyword k of model m, which names one row when the app's
// migrations make that field unique (rps_unique_lookup).
.decl rps_single(e: node, h: node)
rps_single(e, h) :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, a), rps_one_row_method(a),
    rps_from(o, h, _, "rows").
rps_single(e, h) :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, a), (a = "filter" ; a = "get"),
    call_arg(e, -1, k, _), rps_from(o, h, _, "rows"), (k = "pk" ; k = "id" ; k = "pk__exact" ; k = "id__exact").
rps_single(e, h) :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, a), rps_chain_method(a), rps_single(o, h).
rps_single(e, h) :- kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, y), look(e, y, h), rps_single_name(h, y).
rps_single(e, h) :- kind(e, "parenthesized_expression"), unparen(e, u), rps_single(u, h).
.decl rps_single_name(h: node, y: symbol)
rps_single_name(h, y) :- asg(h, y, v, _), unparen(v, e), rps_single(e, h).
.decl rps_single_if(e: node, h: node, m: symbol, k: symbol)
rps_single_if(e, h, m, k) :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, a), (a = "filter" ; a = "get"),
    call_arg(e, -1, k, _), k != "", rps_from(o, h, m, "rows").
rps_single_if(e, h, m, k) :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, a), rps_chain_method(a),
    rps_single_if(o, h, m, k).
rps_single_if(e, h, m, k) :- kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, y), look(e, y, h), rps_single_name_if(h, y, m, k).
rps_single_if(e, h, m, k) :- kind(e, "parenthesized_expression"), unparen(e, u), rps_single_if(u, h, m, k).
.decl rps_single_name_if(h: node, y: symbol, m: symbol, k: symbol)
rps_single_name_if(h, y, m, k) :- asg(h, y, v, _), unparen(v, e), rps_single_if(e, h, m, k).
.decl rps_one_row_method(a: symbol)
rps_one_row_method("get"). rps_one_row_method("first"). rps_one_row_method("last"). rps_one_row_method("latest").
rps_one_row_method("earliest").
// rps_unique_lookup(m, k): keyword k of a filter on model m names one row: a field the run's migrations declare
// unique (`unique=True`, `primary_key=True`, a OneToOneField), bare or with `__exact` (a OneToOneField also as
// `<name>_id`). rps_unique_field(m, x), rps_o2o_field(m, x): stated in each migration's file.
.decl rps_unique_field(m: symbol, x: symbol)
rps_unique_field(m, x) :- dj_field_def(p, _, _, m, x), dj_mig_field(p, x, f, t), (t = "OneToOneField" ;
    call_arg(f, -1, "unique", v), kind(v, "true") ; call_arg(f, -1, "primary_key", v), kind(v, "true")).
.decl rps_o2o_field(m: symbol, x: symbol)
rps_o2o_field(m, x) :- dj_field_def(p, _, _, m, x), dj_mig_field(p, x, _, "OneToOneField").
.decl rps_unique_lookup(m: symbol, k: symbol)
rps_unique_lookup(m, k) :- rps_unique_field(m, x), (k = x ; k = cat(x, "__exact")).
rps_unique_lookup(m, cat(x, "_id")) :- rps_o2o_field(m, x).
// rps_one(k, i, q, h, c): write c of def h touches one row once when RunPython item i of migration k runs q: one row
// in h's code, and h not called from a loop of q.
.decl rps_one(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol, h: symbol, c: symbol)
rps_one(k, i, q, h, c) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_w_one(h, c, "", ""), !rps_looped(k, i, q, h).
rps_one(k, i, q, h, c) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_w_one(h, c, um, uk), rps_unique_lookup(um, uk),
    !rps_looped(k, i, q, h).
// rps_bulk(k, i, q, m): that RunPython writes rows of m other than one row once.
.decl rps_bulk(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_bulk(k, i, q, m) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_w(h, c, m), !rps_one(k, i, q, h, c).

// ---- foreign keys --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rps_fk_field(m, x): model m (lowercased) has foreign key x, in the run's migrations or models.
.decl rps_fk_field(m: symbol, x: symbol)
rps_fk_field(m, x) :- dj_mig_field(op, x, _, t), dj_fk_class(t), dj_mig_model(op, m).
rps_fk_field(@lower(n), x) :- dj_field(c, x, _, t), dj_fk_class(t), def_name(c, n).
// rps_rel(e, j, m, t): an operation at item j of migration e adds a foreign key or many-to-many field of model m that
// points at model t; rps_m2m(e, j, m): a many-to-many field of m (its join table points back at m).
.decl rps_rel(e: symbol, j: number, m: symbol, t: symbol)
rps_rel(e, j, m, t) :- dj_mig_db_op(op, _, _, j), dj_mig_field(op, _, f, c), (dj_fk_class(c) ; c = "ManyToManyField"),
    dj_mig_model(op, m), rps_target(f, t), dj_key_of(op, e).
.decl rps_m2m(e: symbol, j: number, m: symbol)
rps_m2m(e, j, m) :- dj_mig_db_op(op, _, _, j), dj_mig_field(op, _, _, "ManyToManyField"), dj_mig_model(op, m),
    dj_key_of(op, e).
// rps_target(f, m): relation call f (rps_rel_call) points at model m (lowercased): `to="app.M"`, `to="M"`, the first
// positional argument, or settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL ("user").
.decl rps_target(f: node, m: symbol)
rps_target(f, @lower(n)) :- rps_rel_call(f), (call_arg(f, -1, "to", v) ; posarg(f, 0, v)), str(v, s), split_dot(s, _, n).
rps_target(f, @lower(s)) :- rps_rel_call(f), (call_arg(f, -1, "to", v) ; posarg(f, 0, v)), str(v, s), !contains(".", s).
rps_target(f, "user") :- rps_rel_call(f), (call_arg(f, -1, "to", v) ; posarg(f, 0, v)), sym_of(v, q),
    suffix("AUTH_USER_MODEL", q).
// rps_rel_call(f): f is a foreign key or many-to-many field call of a migration operation.
.decl rps_rel_call(f: node)
rps_rel_call(f) :- dj_mig_field(_, _, f, c), (dj_fk_class(c) ; c = "ManyToManyField").
// rps_referenced(k, i, q, m): when RunPython item i of migration k runs q, which deletes rows of m, a foreign key or
// many-to-many field points at m, or m declares a many-to-many field: a field an operation of an earlier migration of
// the app, or an earlier operation of k, adds.
.decl rps_referenced(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_referenced(k, i, q, m) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_del(h, m), rps_rel(e, j, _, m),
    (dj_mig_ran_before(e, k) ; e = k, j < i).
rps_referenced(k, i, q, m) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_del(h, m), rps_m2m(e, j, m),
    (dj_mig_ran_before(e, k) ; e = k, j < i).
// rps_queues(k, i, q, m, x): that RunPython writes rows of m that queue deferred foreign-key checks on m's table: it
// inserts rows into a model with a deferred foreign key, or deletes rows a foreign key can point at (x is "*": any
// constraint), or sets deferred foreign key x.
.decl rps_queues(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol, m: symbol, x: symbol)
rps_queues(k, i, q, m, "*") :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_ins(h, m), rps_deferred_fk(k, i, q, m, _, _).
rps_queues(k, i, q, m, "*") :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_del(h, m), rps_referenced(k, i, q, m).
rps_queues(k, i, q, m, x) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_set(h, m, a), rps_deferred_fk(k, i, q, m, x, a).
rps_queues(k, i, q, m, x) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_save(h, m), rps_def(k, i, q, g), rps_assign(g, m, t),
    rps_deferred_fk(k, i, q, m, x, t).
// rps_deferred_fk(k, i, q, m, x, a): model m, which that RunPython writes, holds deferred foreign key x in attribute a
// (`x`, `x_id`) when it runs. A foreign key an AddField earlier in the same migration added is not deferred: Django's
// PostgreSQL backend adds it with `SET CONSTRAINTS … IMMEDIATE` (rps_added_before).
.decl rps_deferred_fk(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol, m: symbol, x: symbol, a: symbol)
rps_deferred_fk(k, i, q, m, x, x) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_w(h, _, m), rps_fk_field(m, x),
    !rps_added_before(k, i, m, x).
rps_deferred_fk(k, i, q, m, x, cat(x, "_id")) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_w(h, _, m), rps_fk_field(m, x),
    !rps_added_before(k, i, m, x).
// rps_added_before(k, i, m, x): an AddField before RunPython item i of migration k adds field x of model m. Stated in
// k's file.
.decl rps_added_before(k: symbol, i: number, m: symbol, x: symbol)
rps_added_before(k, i, m, x) :- rps_rp(o, d, i, _), dj_mig_db_op(p, "AddField", d, j), j < i, dj_mig_model(p, m),
    dj_mig_arg(p, "name", n), str(n, x), dj_key_of(o, k).

// ---- the schema changes ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rps_alter_kind(k): the operations that alter an existing table (ALTER TABLE, or an index on it).
.decl rps_alter_kind(k: symbol)
rps_alter_kind("AddField"). rps_alter_kind("AlterField"). rps_alter_kind("RemoveField"). rps_alter_kind("RenameField").
rps_alter_kind("AddIndex"). rps_alter_kind("RemoveIndex"). rps_alter_kind("RenameIndex").
rps_alter_kind("AddConstraint"). rps_alter_kind("RemoveConstraint"). rps_alter_kind("AlterUniqueTogether").
rps_alter_kind("AlterIndexTogether"). rps_alter_kind("AlterModelTable"). rps_alter_kind("RenameModel").
rps_alter_kind("DeleteModel").

// rps_alter(s, c, j, m): operation s of class c, item j of its migration, alters model m's table (a RenameModel under
// its old and its new name).
.decl rps_alter(s: node, c: symbol, j: number, m: symbol)
rps_alter(s, c, j, m) :- dj_mig_db_op(s, c, _, j), rps_alter_kind(c), dj_mig_model(s, m).
rps_alter(s, "RenameModel", j, @lower(t)) :- dj_mig_db_op(s, "RenameModel", _, j), dj_mig_arg(s, "new_name", n),
    str(n, t).
// rps_flushes(s, x): AlterField or RemoveField s changes foreign key x itself: Django's PostgreSQL backend first runs
// `SET CONSTRAINTS <its constraint> IMMEDIATE`, which runs that constraint's queued checks, and then drops it.
.decl rps_flushes(s: node, x: symbol)
rps_flushes(s, x) :- (dj_mig_db_op(s, "AlterField", _, _) ; dj_mig_db_op(s, "RemoveField", _, _)),
    dj_mig_arg(s, "name", n), str(n, x).
// rps_alt(k, j, m, x, c): by key, an operation of class c at item j of migration k alters model m's table; x is the
// field it changes itself (rps_flushes), else "".
.decl rps_alt(k: symbol, j: number, m: symbol, x: symbol, c: symbol)
rps_alt(k, j, m, x, c) :- rps_alter(s, c, j, m), rps_flushes(s, x), dj_key_of(s, k).
rps_alt(k, j, m, "", c) :- rps_alter(s, c, j, m), !rps_flushes(s, _), dj_key_of(s, k).
// rps_live_alt(k, j, m, x): such an operation runs SQL: other than an AlterField that changes only attributes Django
// keeps out of the database (rps_noop).
.decl rps_live_alt(k: symbol, j: number, m: symbol, x: symbol)
rps_live_alt(k, j, m, x) :- rps_alt(k, j, m, x, c), c != "AlterField".
rps_live_alt(k, j, m, x) :- rps_alt(k, j, m, x, "AlterField"), !rps_noop(k, j, m, x).

// rps_noop(d, i, m, x): the AlterField of model m's field x at item i of migration d changes only attributes Django
// keeps out of the database (choices, help_text, verbose_name, blank, default, ...): its field call has the class of
// the field's nearest earlier definition in the app's migrations (dj_field_src, as
// django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table reads it) and differs from it in no other argument, so it runs no SQL.
// Each migration file describes its field calls by values for this (rps_fc).
.decl rps_noop(d: symbol, i: number, m: symbol, x: symbol)
rps_noop(d, i, m, x) :- dj_field_src(d, i, m, x, e, j, y), rps_vcls(d, i, m, x, "new", t), rps_vcls(e, j, m, y, "def", t),
    !rps_db_diff(d, i, m, x, e, j, y).
// rps_nondb(k): field arguments that change no column (Field.non_db_attrs, and `default`, which Django keeps out of
// the database unless a null column becomes NOT NULL, a change of `null` that counts anyway).
.decl rps_nondb(k: symbol)
rps_nondb("blank"). rps_nondb("choices"). rps_nondb("editable"). rps_nondb("error_messages"). rps_nondb("help_text").
rps_nondb("limit_choices_to"). rps_nondb("on_delete"). rps_nondb("related_name"). rps_nondb("related_query_name").
rps_nondb("validators"). rps_nondb("verbose_name"). rps_nondb("default").
// rps_fc(f, e, j, m, x, w): field call f is described under key (e, j, m, x, w): w "new", the field of an AlterField
// at item j of migration e, a migration with a RunPython this rule reads; w "def", a definition's field call.
.decl rps_fc(f: node, e: symbol, j: number, m: symbol, x: symbol, w: symbol)
rps_fc(f, e, j, m, x, "new") :- dj_alterfield(s, d, j, m, x), rps_rp(_, d, _, _), dj_mig_arg(s, "field", f),
    dj_key_of(f, e).
rps_fc(f, e, j, m, x, "def") :- dj_field_def(p, _, j, m, x), dj_mig_field(p, x, f, _), dj_key_of(f, e).
// rps_vcls(…, t): the call's class t (its last name); rps_vkw(…, k, v): its keyword argument k, one that changes the
// column, of text v; rps_vpos(…, n, v): its positional argument n, of text v.
.decl rps_vcls(e: symbol, j: number, m: symbol, x: symbol, w: symbol, t: symbol)
rps_vcls(e, j, m, x, w, t) :- rps_fc(f, e, j, m, x, w), dj_mig_field_class(f, t).
.decl rps_vkw(e: symbol, j: number, m: symbol, x: symbol, w: symbol, k: symbol, v: symbol)
rps_vkw(e, j, m, x, w, k, v) :- rps_fc(f, e, j, m, x, w), call_arg(f, -1, k, a), k != "", !rps_nondb(k), text(a, v).
.decl rps_vpos(e: symbol, j: number, m: symbol, x: symbol, w: symbol, n: number, v: symbol)
rps_vpos(e, j, m, x, w, n, v) :- rps_fc(f, e, j, m, x, w), posarg(f, n, a), text(a, v).
// rps_db_diff(d, i, m, x, e, j, y): the AlterField's call and the definition's differ in an argument that changes the
// column.
.decl rps_db_diff(d: symbol, i: number, m: symbol, x: symbol, e: symbol, j: number, y: symbol)
rps_db_diff(d, i, m, x, e, j, y) :- dj_field_src(d, i, m, x, e, j, y), rps_vkw(d, i, m, x, "new", k, v),
    !rps_vkw(e, j, m, y, "def", k, v).
rps_db_diff(d, i, m, x, e, j, y) :- dj_field_src(d, i, m, x, e, j, y), rps_vkw(e, j, m, y, "def", k, v),
    !rps_vkw(d, i, m, x, "new", k, v).
rps_db_diff(d, i, m, x, e, j, y) :- dj_field_src(d, i, m, x, e, j, y), rps_vpos(d, i, m, x, "new", n, v),
    !rps_vpos(e, j, m, y, "def", n, v).
rps_db_diff(d, i, m, x, e, j, y) :- dj_field_src(d, i, m, x, e, j, y), rps_vpos(e, j, m, y, "def", n, v),
    !rps_vpos(d, i, m, x, "new", n, v).

// rps_sql_imm(k, j): `SET CONSTRAINTS ALL IMMEDIATE` runs, in a RunSQL of migration k, before its item j. It runs
// every queued check, and the checks of later writes in the transaction at once (DefectDojo's
// `0286_cicd_infrastructure.py`). Stated in k's file. rps_code_imm(k, i, q): a string of that RunPython's own code
// runs it.
.decl rps_sql_imm(k: symbol, j: number)
rps_sql_imm(k, j) :- dj_mig_db_op(r, "RunSQL", d, kk), dj_mig_arg(r, "sql", v), (str(v, t) ; child(v, s, _), str(s, t)),
    match("(?is).*set\\s+constraints\\s+all\\s+immediate.*", t), dj_mig_db_op(a, _, d, j), kk < j, dj_key_of(a, k).
.decl rps_code_imm(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol)
rps_code_imm(k, i, q) :- rps_def(k, i, q, h), rps_sets_all(h).
// rps_creates(k, m): migration k creates model m.
.decl rps_creates(k: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_creates(k, m) :- dj_mig_db_op(o, "CreateModel", _, _), dj_mig_model(o, m), dj_key_of(o, k).

// ---- the two orders ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rps_after(k, i, q, m): RunPython item i of migration k, running q, queues foreign-key checks on m's table, and a
// later operation alters that table (other than one that runs those checks first, rps_flushes), with no SET
// CONSTRAINTS ALL IMMEDIATE between.
.decl rps_after(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_after(k, i, q, m) :- rps_queues(k, i, q, m, x), rps_live_alt(k, j, m, fx), j > i, !rps_creates(k, m), fx != x,
    !rps_sql_imm(k, j), !rps_code_imm(k, i, q).
// rps_before(k, i, q, m): an earlier operation altered m's table, and that RunPython then writes its rows (other than
// one row once), and the project's code does not read m as one row (dj_one_row: a settings table).
.decl rps_before(k: symbol, i: number, q: symbol, m: symbol)
rps_before(k, i, q, m) :- rps_bulk(k, i, q, m), rps_live_alt(k, j, m, _), j < i, !rps_creates(k, m), !dj_one_row(m).

// The cases, `cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/`, read as one repository: each line ending in
// `# caught` is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "shop/backfills.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/backfills.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0001_initial.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0001_initial.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0001_squashed_0002_order_number.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0001_squashed_0002_order_number.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0002_order_number.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0002_order_number.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0003_merge_customers.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0003_merge_customers.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0004_product_price_cents.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0004_product_price_cents.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0005_customer_email_index.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0005_customer_email_index.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0006_walk_in_order.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0006_walk_in_order.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0007_tag_rename.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0007_tag_rename.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0008_nonatomic.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0008_nonatomic.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0009_read_and_other_model.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0009_read_and_other_model.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0010_coupon.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0010_coupon.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0011_sql_state_noop.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0011_sql_state_noop.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0012_dynamic_model.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0012_dynamic_model.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0013_no_pending_checks.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0013_no_pending_checks.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0014_order_coupon.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0014_order_coupon.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0015_customer_tier.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0015_customer_tier.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0016_sitesettings.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0016_sitesettings.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0017_tag_order_protect.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0017_tag_order_protect.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0018_tag_product.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0018_tag_product.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0019_customer_status.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0019_customer_status.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0020_drop_blank_customers.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0020_drop_blank_customers.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0021_drop_unnamed_customers.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0021_drop_unnamed_customers.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0022_drop_guest_customers.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0022_drop_guest_customers.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0023_loop_models.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0023_loop_models.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0024_customer_flags.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/migrations/0024_customer_flags.py"
    .fixture "shop/models.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/models.py"
    .fixture "shop/settings.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/settings.py"
    .fixture "shop/tests/migrations/0001_fixture.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/tests/migrations/0001_fixture.py"
    .fixture "shop/tests_e2e/e2e_test_checkout.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/tests_e2e/e2e_test_checkout.py"
    .fixture "shop/views.py" from "../cases/django-practice-runpython-with-schema-change/shop/views.py"
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0002_order_number.py":21
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_merge_customers.py":22
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0004_product_price_cents.py":16
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0005_customer_email_index.py":20
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0006_walk_in_order.py":16
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0007_tag_rename.py":20
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0014_order_coupon.py":21
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0019_customer_status.py":30
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0022_drop_guest_customers.py":14
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0023_loop_models.py":16
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0024_customer_flags.py":41
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0024_customer_flags.py":42
.end
